  "_source": "Hand-verified directly against RCA-DFC-REG-002.md Section 29 (0x4000-0x4058) per-field bit tables, cited by contract ID, and RCA-DFC-ARCH-002.md's dfc_rtl022_control_t/status_t Appendix B tables. Covers all 23 real RTL-022 registers -- REG-002's own block header (Section 29) says 23 and the block lists exactly 23 rows (confirmed by direct count); RTL-022_RevA.md's own stale claims (11 ports -- real is 35, confirmed against ARCH-002 Appendix A directly; 20 registers -- real is 23) are both wrong, disclosed in OPEN_ISSUES.md, not followed. ULI_IO_DIRECTION (0x4040, CONST, fixed zero, ACCESS_ERROR on any write) needs no field-map entry at all -- handled generically by reggen.py's own CONST readback class. ULI_IN_LEVEL/ULI_OUT_LEVEL/ULI_OUT_DATA/ULI_IO_INPUT are pure-RO registers (status_registers entries only, no control_registers entry, same precedent as UART_RX_LEVEL/CAN_RX_ID/etc. in rtl019/020_field_map.json). ULI_PARAM0-7/ULI_IN_DATA/ULI_IO_OUTPUT are plain RW registers forwarded to RTL-022 via control_registers only (no status_registers entry -- dfc_rtl022_status_t has no corresponding readback field for any of these at all, confirmed directly: the generic regbank's own existing stored-value echo is this register's own readback, the same already-disclosed, pre-existing RTL-001 gap named in every prior module's own header -- 'no per-field legal-value range checks' -- not a new gap invented for this module; see OPEN_ISSUES.md for the explicit disclosure that REG-002's own 'reads zero' prose for these registers is therefore not literally enforced at the register level, only RTL-022's OWN internal violation-detection-and-ignore behavior is real). A genuine, disclosed REG-002-internal inconsistency was found and resolved while building this field map: ULI_CONTROL's own 'Register behavior' prose says 'ENABLE and IRQ_ENABLE have the sole legal value zero,' directly contradicting its OWN per-field 'Legal values/range' column ('0 or 1' for both, with no 'in Revision A' qualifier the OTHER real zero-only fields in this same section all consistently carry) -- resolved in favor of the prose (ENABLE/IRQ_ENABLE DO get the same reject-nonzero-plus-violation-evidence treatment as the 8 parameters and OUTPUT_REQUEST), per ARCH-002's own ARCH-ULI-001 ('Any nonzero parameter write or enable attempt is rejected and sets violation evidence') and this session's own task briefing explicitly requiring 'ENABLE/IRQ_ENABLE nonzero-write rejection (REG-ENC-017)' -- REG-ENC-017's own literal text names only 'functional enable' (ENABLE) explicitly, not IRQ_ENABLE by name, so IRQ_ENABLE's own inclusion rests on REG-002's own ULI_CONTROL prose plus this session's explicit instruction, not REG-ENC-017's own narrower literal wording -- disclosed, not silently picked, in OPEN_ISSUES.md. EVENT_ENABLE is NOT part of this restriction (REG-002's own prose: 'diagnostic EVENT_ENABLE remain available'), an ordinary RW bit.",
